(media/'narration.txt').write_text('Before rebuilding a VPS, decide which state you want to create. The ConoHa guide describes server rebuilding as overwriting the existing server with an operating system installation. Existing data is not automatically carried forward. It distinguishes operating system images, application images, saved images, and automatic backup sources. A new operating system and a saved state are different choices. Our saveable decision sheet connects the purpose, the selected source, the target server, the data that must remain, the configuration that must be recreated, and the service checks after rebuilding. Leave unknown items blank. A saved image name alone does not prove that the required state can be recreated. Record the service result you need before the work. After the owners separately confirmed operation, distinguish completion of rebuilding from verification of the necessary data and application behavior. The reference cost uses an assumed duration and a published base rate. It is not a rebuild fee or a measured recovery time. No server was reinstalled for this guide.',encoding='utf-8')
